<title>USA: Family Bargain names chairman, seeks CFO.</title>
<headline>Family Bargain names chairman, seeks CFO.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Family Bargain Corp Tuesday said it has named James Sommerville as its chairman, and said that executive vice president Jeffrey Gertsel has resigned.</p>
<p>The company said it will immediately begin to search for a new chief financial officer.  </p>
<p>Somerville had been executive vice-president of BET Inc, the U.S. unit of BET Plc.</p>
<p>Family Bargain did not say who he replaces as chairman. The company was not immediately available for comment.</p>
